#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Deterministic confidence-interval engine forensics audit.

Study: anonymous_bootstrap_ci_engine_forensics (task computer_science.bci_forensics)

All evidence comes from the supplied files in data/; no resampling panels are
regenerated and engine/case identity is taken from the explicit ``engine_ids``
/ ``case_ids`` arrays stored in engine_interval_panels.npz (never row order).

Public statistic definitions (from study_manifest.json):
  mean                     : sample mean
  median                   : sample median
  coefficient_of_variation : sample std (ddof=1) / sample mean
  upper_tail_rate          : fraction of observations >= threshold (threshold=4, ">=")

Population target (declared convention, kept fixed):
  theta_hat(case) = mean over the 108 calibration replications of the statistic
  computed on each replication sample (plug-in Monte-Carlo estimate of the
  population parameter).  Deterministic; uses only supplied calibration data.

Coverage diagnostics (calibration replications, n=108 per case):
  empirical_coverage : fraction of reps with low <= theta_hat <= high
  miss_low_rate      : fraction with theta_hat < low
  miss_high_rate     : fraction with theta_hat > high
  mean_width         : mean(high - low)
  coverage_score     : |emp - nominal| + |miss_low - miss_high|  (higher = worse)

Probe-family semantics (all diagnostic_value entries are finite SEVERITY
measures; larger = worse; the scale is this audit's own and is kept mutually
consistent across every output table):
  probe_00 coverage-asymmetry : per-case |emp-nominal| + |miss_low-miss_high|
      (derived from calibration evidence; equals the per-case coverage_score).
  probe_01 width/shape        : per-case |engine_width - baseline_width| /
      baseline_width (derived from calibration evidence vs the supplied
      baseline percentile interval).
  probe_02 scale-response     : supplied probe_panel_02 endpoints.  Response
      delta = (panel - observed) endpoints; severity = max absolute deviation
      of the engine's delta from the CROSS-ENGINE CONSENSUS (median) delta.
      ORIENTATION DECLARATION / AMBIGUITY FLAG: engines 03 and 06 are exactly
      invariant under this panel while all other engines respond.  Under the
      declared orientation an atypical response (including zero response) is
      severity.  This orientation is used consistently everywhere and is
      explicitly flagged in reliability_report case warnings where relevant.
  probe_03 split-noise        : supplied probe_panel_03 endpoints (6 splits =
      study split_count).  Severity = mean across splits of the std of the low
      and high endpoints (direct noise-amplification measure).
  probe_04 reflection         : observed-case reflection asymmetry
      |(theta - low) - (high - theta)| compared against the baseline's own
      asymmetry: severity = |asym_engine - asym_baseline| (excess asymmetry).

Engine audit aggregates (mean over the 6 public cases):
  coverage_gap   : mean(nominal - empirical)                [signed; |.| in scoring]
  tail_imbalance : mean |miss_low - miss_high|
  width_ratio    : mean(engine mean_width / baseline width) [|ratio-1| in scoring]
  case_dispersion: cross-case dispersion of the engine's own behavior =
                   std over cases of (nominal - empirical coverage) +
                   std over cases of (mean width / baseline width); engines
                   that collapse on specific regimes are penalized.
  probe_metric_kk: mean over cases of family kk diagnostic_value
  engine_score   : HIGHER = MORE RELIABLE.  Weighted sum of per-component
      reliability 1 - minmax(severity) across engines with fixed weights:
      coverage_gap .18, tail_imbalance .14, width_ratio .08, case_dispersion
      .10, baseline_alias .10 (always-on block, belongs to no probe family)
      and .08 per probe family (.40 total).  The baseline_alias severity is
      clip(1 - d_base/0.10, 0, 1) with
      d_base = mean over cases of max|endpoint - baseline|/baseline_width:
      an engine that merely reproduces the supplied baseline interval is not
      a reliable engine.  Degenerate (zero-range) components contribute no
      penalty (component reliability = 1).

Family ablation reuses exactly the combined-score definition above: for each
excluded probe family that family's 0.08-weight term is dropped and the score
is renormalized by the remaining total weight; the coverage blocks and the
always-on baseline_alias block are kept.  The ``none`` row uses the full score
(identical to engine_audit.engine_score ranking).

Failure evidence scores (per engine, finite, larger = more supporting evidence):
  reliable_engine           : engine_score (the combined reliability score)
  baseline_quantile_alias   : closeness of observed endpoints to the supplied
                              baseline interval: clip(1 - d/0.10, 0, 1) with
                              d = mean_cases max|endpoint - baseline|/width
  reflection_alias          : minmax(mean probe_04 severity)
  discrete_boundary_mismatch: case_03 (discrete_tie) evidence: minmax of
      0.5*P(low<0) + 0.25*P(high>1) + 0.25*|coverage gap| on case_03
  shape_correction_mismatch : minmax of mean severity over the ratio (case_02)
      and median (case_05) cases: |coverage gap| + 0.5*probe_01 severity
  scale_response_mismatch   : minmax(mean probe_02 severity)
  noise_amplifying_engine   : 0.6*minmax(mean probe_03 severity)
                              + 0.4*minmax(case_dispersion)
  Predicted label = argmax evidence score per engine (ties broken by the fixed
  vocabulary order); labels may repeat across engines.

case_warnings thresholds: coverage gap > 0.05, tail imbalance > 0.05, any
diagnostic_score >= 0.8, width ratio outside [0.8, 1.25].  Where a probe_02
warning triggers, the orientation ambiguity is restated in the warning text.
"""
import json
import os

import numpy as np

try:  # matplotlib preferred; Pillow fallback keeps the PNG reproducible anywhere
    import matplotlib
    matplotlib.use("Agg")
    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
    HAVE_MPL = True
except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover - exercised when matplotlib is absent
    HAVE_MPL = False

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

DATA = "data"
OUT = "results"
os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)

MAN = json.load(open(os.path.join(DATA, "study_manifest.json")))
PROBE_MAN = json.load(open(os.path.join(DATA, "probe_manifest.json")))
CONF = MAN["confidence_level"]
CASES = [c["case_id"] for c in MAN["cases"]]
META = {c["case_id"]: c for c in MAN["cases"]}
ENGINES = list(MAN["engine_ids"])
LABELS = list(MAN["failure_label_vocabulary"])
PROBES = list(PROBE_MAN["probe_families"])

panels = np.load(os.path.join(DATA, "engine_interval_panels.npz"), allow_pickle=True)
assert list(panels["engine_ids"]) == ENGINES
assert list(panels["case_ids"]) == CASES
cal_samples = np.load(os.path.join(DATA, "calibration_samples.npz"), allow_pickle=True)
resample_panels = np.load(os.path.join(DATA, "resample_panels.npz"), allow_pickle=True)
obs_df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA, "observed_samples.csv"))

NENG, NCASE = len(ENGINES), len(CASES)
NOM = CONF


def statistic(x, name, params):
    if name == "mean":
        return x.mean(-1)
    if name == "median":
        return np.median(x, -1)
    if name == "coefficient_of_variation":
        return x.std(-1, ddof=params.get("std_ddof", 1)) / x.mean(-1)
    if name == "upper_tail_rate":
        thr = params["threshold"]
        if params.get("comparison", ">=") != ">=":
            raise ValueError("unsupported comparison")
        return (x >= thr).mean(-1)
    raise ValueError(name)


OBS_VALUES = {c: obs_df[obs_df.case_id == c]["value"].to_numpy(float) for c in CASES}
OBS_STAT = np.array([
    float(statistic(OBS_VALUES[c], META[c]["statistic_name"], META[c]["statistic_parameters"]))
    for c in CASES
])
assert np.allclose(OBS_STAT, panels["observed_stat"]), "observed_stat mismatch"

TARGET = np.array([  # declared plug-in MC population target
    float(statistic(cal_samples[c], META[c]["statistic_name"],
                    META[c]["statistic_parameters"]).mean())
    for c in CASES
])

BASE_LOW, BASE_HIGH = panels["baseline_low"], panels["baseline_high"]
BASE_WIDTH = BASE_HIGH - BASE_LOW
obs_low, obs_high = panels["observed_low"], panels["observed_high"]          # (9,6)
cal_low, cal_high = panels["calibration_low"], panels["calibration_high"]    # (9,6,108)
NREP = cal_low.shape[2]
assert NREP == META["case_00"]["n_calibration_replications"]


# ------------------------------------------------------- coverage audit table
rows = []
emp = np.zeros((NENG, NCASE)); mlow = np.zeros((NENG, NCASE))
mhigh = np.zeros((NENG, NCASE)); mwidth = np.zeros((NENG, NCASE))
for i, c in enumerate(CASES):
    for e in range(NENG):
        lo, hi = cal_low[e, i], cal_high[e, i]
        t = TARGET[i]
        cov = float(((lo <= t) & (hi >= t)).mean())
        ml = float((t < lo).mean()); mh = float((t > hi).mean())
        mw = float((hi - lo).mean())
        emp[e, i], mlow[e, i], mhigh[e, i], mwidth[e, i] = cov, ml, mh, mw
        rows.append(dict(
            case_id=c, regime=META[c]["regime"], engine_id=ENGINES[e],
            nominal_coverage=NOM, empirical_coverage=cov, mean_width=mw,
            miss_low_rate=ml, miss_high_rate=mh, n_replications=NREP,
            coverage_score=abs(cov - NOM) + abs(ml - mh)))
coverage_df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=MAN["audit_columns"]["coverage_audit"])


def minmax(v):
    v = np.asarray(v, float)
    rng = v.max() - v.min()
    return np.zeros_like(v) if rng <= 0 else (v - v.min()) / rng


# ------------------------------------------------- probe diagnostics (9 x 6)
diag = {}
diag["probe_00"] = np.abs(emp - NOM) + np.abs(mlow - mhigh)
diag["probe_01"] = np.abs(mwidth - BASE_WIDTH[None, :]) / BASE_WIDTH[None, :]
d_lo = panels["probe_panel_02_low"] - obs_low
d_hi = panels["probe_panel_02_high"] - obs_high
cons_lo, cons_hi = np.median(d_lo, axis=0), np.median(d_hi, axis=0)
diag["probe_02"] = np.maximum(np.abs(d_lo - cons_lo[None, :]),
                              np.abs(d_hi - cons_hi[None, :]))
p3l, p3h = panels["probe_panel_03_low"], panels["probe_panel_03_high"]
assert p3l.shape[2] == MAN["split_count"]
diag["probe_03"] = 0.5 * (p3l.std(-1) + p3h.std(-1))
asym_e = np.abs((TARGET[None, :] - obs_low) - (obs_high - TARGET[None, :]))
asym_b = np.abs((TARGET - BASE_LOW) - (BASE_HIGH - TARGET))
diag["probe_04"] = np.abs(asym_e - asym_b[None, :])

dscore = {f: np.stack([minmax(diag[f][:, i]) for i in range(NCASE)], axis=1)
          for f in PROBES}

probe_rows = []
for fi, f in enumerate(PROBES):
    for i, c in enumerate(CASES):
        for e in range(NENG):
            probe_rows.append(dict(
                case_id=c, probe_family=f, engine_id=ENGINES[e],
                diagnostic_value=float(diag[f][e, i]),
                diagnostic_score=float(dscore[f][e, i])))
probe_df = pd.DataFrame(probe_rows, columns=PROBE_MAN["diagnostic_columns"])

profile_rows = []
for i, c in enumerate(CASES):
    for e in range(NENG):
        profile_rows.append(dict(
            case_id=c, engine_id=ENGINES[e],
            **{f"probe_signal_{k:02d}": float(diag[PROBES[k]][e, i]) for k in range(5)},
            profile_score=float(np.mean([dscore[PROBES[k]][e, i] for k in range(5)]))))
profile_df = pd.DataFrame(profile_rows, columns=MAN["audit_columns"]["case_probe_profile"])


# ------------------------------------------------------------- engine audit
d_base = np.mean([np.maximum(np.abs(obs_low[:, i] - BASE_LOW[i]),
                             np.abs(obs_high[:, i] - BASE_HIGH[i])) / BASE_WIDTH[i]
                  for i in range(NCASE)], axis=0)
SEV = {
    "coverage_gap": np.abs(emp.mean(1) - NOM),
    "tail_imbalance": np.abs(mlow - mhigh).mean(1),
    "width_ratio": np.abs(mwidth / BASE_WIDTH[None, :] - 1.0).mean(1),
    "case_dispersion": (emp - NOM).std(1) + (mwidth / BASE_WIDTH[None, :]).std(1),
    "baseline_alias": np.clip(1.0 - d_base / 0.10, 0.0, 1.0),
}
for f in PROBES:
    SEV[f] = diag[f].mean(1)

WEIGHTS = [
    ("coverage_gap", 0.18, SEV["coverage_gap"]),
    ("tail_imbalance", 0.14, SEV["tail_imbalance"]),
    ("width_ratio", 0.08, SEV["width_ratio"]),
    ("case_dispersion", 0.10, SEV["case_dispersion"]),
    ("baseline_alias", 0.10, SEV["baseline_alias"]),
    ("probe_00", 0.08, SEV["probe_00"]),
    ("probe_01", 0.08, SEV["probe_01"]),
    ("probe_02", 0.08, SEV["probe_02"]),
    ("probe_03", 0.08, SEV["probe_03"]),
    ("probe_04", 0.08, SEV["probe_04"]),
]


def combined_score(used_weights):
    """Reliability score (higher = better) for a subset of (name, w, severity)."""
    total_w = sum(w for _, w, _ in used_weights)
    s = np.zeros(NENG)
    for _, w, sev in used_weights:
        s += w * (1.0 - minmax(sev))
    return s / total_w


ENGINE_SCORE = combined_score(WEIGHTS)

engine_df = pd.DataFrame(dict(
    engine_id=ENGINES,
    coverage_gap=(NOM - emp).mean(1),
    tail_imbalance=np.abs(mlow - mhigh).mean(1),
    width_ratio=(mwidth / BASE_WIDTH[None, :]).mean(1),
    case_dispersion=SEV["case_dispersion"],
    **{f"probe_metric_{k:02d}": SEV[PROBES[k]] for k in range(5)},
    engine_score=ENGINE_SCORE,
))[MAN["audit_columns"]["engine_audit"]]


# ------------------------------------------------------------ family ablation
def ranking(scores):
    order = sorted(range(NENG), key=lambda e: (-scores[e], ENGINES[e]))
    return order, {e: r + 1 for r, e in enumerate(order)}


full_order, full_rank = ranking(ENGINE_SCORE)
SEL = full_order[0]
fam_terms = {f: (0.08, SEV[f]) for f in PROBES}
cover_terms = [(n, w, s) for n, w, s in WEIGHTS if not n.startswith("probe_")]
abl_rows = []
for excl in ["none"] + PROBES:
    terms = WEIGHTS if excl == "none" else cover_terms + [
        (f, w, s) for f, (w, s) in fam_terms.items() if f != excl]
    sc = combined_score(terms)
    order, rank = ranking(sc)
    abl_rows.append(dict(
        excluded_probe_family=excl,
        top_engine_id=ENGINES[order[0]],
        selected_engine_rank=int(rank[SEL]),
        runner_up_engine_id=ENGINES[order[1]],
        score_margin=float(max(sc[order[0]] - sc[order[1]], 0.0))))
ablation_df = pd.DataFrame(abl_rows, columns=MAN["audit_columns"]["family_ablation"])


# ----------------------------------------------------------- failure evidence
p_low_neg = (cal_low[:, 2, :] < 0).mean(1)      # case_03 (discrete_tie)
p_high_gt1 = (cal_high[:, 2, :] > 1).mean(1)
cg_case03 = np.abs(emp[:, 2] - NOM)
discrete_sev = 0.5 * p_low_neg + 0.25 * p_high_gt1 + 0.25 * cg_case03

shape_cases = [i for i, c in enumerate(CASES) if c in ("case_02", "case_05")]
shape_sev = np.mean([np.abs(emp[:, i] - NOM) + 0.5 * diag["probe_01"][:, i]
                     for i in shape_cases], axis=0)

evid = {
    "reliable_engine": ENGINE_SCORE.copy(),
    "baseline_quantile_alias": SEV["baseline_alias"].copy(),
    "reflection_alias": minmax(SEV["probe_04"]),
    "discrete_boundary_mismatch": minmax(discrete_sev),
    "shape_correction_mismatch": minmax(shape_sev),
    "scale_response_mismatch": minmax(SEV["probe_02"]),
    "noise_amplifying_engine": 0.6 * minmax(SEV["probe_03"])
                               + 0.4 * minmax(SEV["case_dispersion"]),
}
ev_rows = []
pred_label = {}
for e in range(NENG):
    scores = sorted(((LABELS.index(l), evid[l][e], l) for l in LABELS),
                    key=lambda t: (-t[1], t[0]))
    pred_label[ENGINES[e]] = scores[0][2]
    for rank, (_, s, l) in enumerate(scores, start=1):
        ev_rows.append(dict(
            engine_id=ENGINES[e], failure_label=l, evidence_score=float(s),
            label_rank=rank, is_predicted_label=1 if rank == 1 else 0))
evidence_df = pd.DataFrame(ev_rows, columns=MAN["audit_columns"]["failure_evidence"])

failure_modes = {"selected_engine_id": ENGINES[SEL],
                 "failure_modes": {eng: pred_label[eng] for eng in ENGINES}}
selected_json = {"selected_engine_id": ENGINES[SEL],
                 "selected_failure_mode": pred_label[ENGINES[SEL]],
                 "selected_engine_score": float(ENGINE_SCORE[SEL])}

# --------------------------------------------------------- interval summary
sel_low, sel_high = obs_low[SEL], obs_high[SEL]
interval_df = pd.DataFrame(dict(
    case_id=CASES,
    statistic_name=[META[c]["statistic_name"] for c in CASES],
    observed_stat=OBS_STAT,
    selected_engine_id=ENGINES[SEL],
    selected_low=sel_low, selected_high=sel_high,
    baseline_low=BASE_LOW, baseline_high=BASE_HIGH,
    selected_width=sel_high - sel_low,
    baseline_width_ratio=(sel_high - sel_low) / BASE_WIDTH,
))

# ------------------------------------------------------- reliability report
sel_diag_scores = np.stack([dscore[f][SEL] for f in PROBES])
case_warnings = {}
for i, c in enumerate(CASES):
    w = []
    if NOM - emp[SEL, i] > 0.05:
        w.append(f"coverage_gap_{NOM - emp[SEL, i]:.3f}_exceeds_0.05")
    if abs(mlow[SEL, i] - mhigh[SEL, i]) > 0.05:
        w.append(f"tail_imbalance_{abs(mlow[SEL, i] - mhigh[SEL, i]):.3f}_exceeds_0.05")
    wr = (sel_high[i] - sel_low[i]) / BASE_WIDTH[i]
    if wr < 0.8 or wr > 1.25:
        w.append(f"baseline_width_ratio_{wr:.3f}_outside_[0.8,1.25]")
    for fi, f in enumerate(PROBES):
        if dscore[f][SEL, i] >= 0.8:
            note = (" (probe_02 orientation ambiguity: atypical-vs-consensus response"
                    " treated as severity; declared orientation kept)"
                    if f == "probe_02" else "")
            w.append(f"{f}_diagnostic_score_{dscore[f][SEL, i]:.3f}_ge_0.8{note}")
    case_warnings[c] = w

report = {
    "selected_engine_id": ENGINES[SEL],
    "aggregate_coverage_gap": float(engine_df.iloc[SEL]["coverage_gap"]),
    "aggregate_tail_imbalance": float(engine_df.iloc[SEL]["tail_imbalance"]),
    "aggregate_probe_score": float(sel_diag_scores.mean()),
    "engine_ranking": [ENGINES[e] for e in full_order],
    "case_warnings": case_warnings,
}

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ figure
def render_png_mpl():
    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(12, 9))
    order = full_order
    ax = axes[0, 0]
    ax.bar([ENGINES[e] for e in order], [ENGINE_SCORE[e] for e in order],
           color=["#2a9d8f" if e == SEL else "#4c72b0" for e in order])
    ax.set_ylabel("engine_score (higher = more reliable)")
    ax.set_title("Combined engine reliability ranking")
    ax.tick_params(axis="x", rotation=45)

    ax = axes[0, 1]
    for e in range(NENG):
        ax.plot(CASES, emp[e], "o-", alpha=0.6,
                color="#2a9d8f" if e == SEL else None)
    ax.axhline(NOM, color="crimson", ls="--", label=f"nominal {NOM}")
    ax.set_ylabel("empirical coverage")
    ax.set_title("Per-case empirical coverage by engine")
    ax.legend(fontsize=7)
    ax.tick_params(axis="x", rotation=45)

    ax = axes[1, 0]
    heat = np.stack([dscore[f].mean(1) for f in PROBES], axis=1)
    im = ax.imshow(heat, aspect="auto", cmap="viridis")
    ax.set_xticks(range(len(PROBES)), PROBES, rotation=45)
    ax.set_yticks(range(NENG), ENGINES)
    ax.set_title("Mean normalized probe diagnostic (severity)")
    fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, shrink=0.8)

    ax = axes[1, 1]
    for e in range(NENG):
        ax.plot(CASES, mwidth[e] / BASE_WIDTH, "o-", alpha=0.6,
                color="#2a9d8f" if e == SEL else None)
    ax.axhline(1.0, color="crimson", ls="--", label="baseline width")
    ax.set_ylabel("mean width / baseline width")
    ax.set_title("Interval width relative to baseline")
    ax.legend(fontsize=7)
    ax.tick_params(axis="x", rotation=45)

    fig.suptitle(f"Anonymous CI-engine audit - selected: {ENGINES[SEL]} "
                 f"(score {ENGINE_SCORE[SEL]:.3f}, label {pred_label[ENGINES[SEL]]})")
    fig.tight_layout()
    fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUT, "engine_overview.png"), dpi=150)
    plt.close(fig)


